    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABJUYpfg",
      "title": "feat: enforce review period delay ranges and lockbox consistency",
      "author": "0xarktos",
      "number": 1374,
      "body": "## Description\r\n\r\nAdds validation for the per-chain review period delays (proof maturity, dispute game finality and DelayedWETH delay) introduced in ethereum-optimism/optimism#23215 and ethereum-optimism/optimism#23215\r\n\r\nThe standard ranges for these delays are widened to the configured bounds and a range is added for the DelayedWETH delay. The staging compliance report now shows the delays of a new chain against those ranges, and a new check groups every registered chain by `ETHLockbox` and asserts that the delays are within range and identical across chains sharing a lockbox, including those in the interop set.\r\n\r\n## Changes\r\n\r\n- `validation`: `proof_maturity_delay_seconds` is `[86400, 604800]`, `dispute_game_finality_delay_seconds` is `[43200, 302400]`, and a new `[delayed_weth] delay_seconds = [43200, 604800]` table and `DelayedWETHParams` struct are added. The bounds match `op-deployer`'s `standard` package and `StandardValidatorUtils.sol`. `Range.WithinRange`, previously unused, get a test.\r\n- `ops/internal/report`: `ScanL1` reads the three delays via a new `ScanReviewPeriod` and the comment template renders a \"Review Period Delays\" block. Both delays are read from the OptimismPortal, which keeps a legacy `disputeGameFinalityDelaySeconds()` forwarding to the AnchorStateRegistry on every release, so no release gating is needed. `checkmarkRangeUint64` now delegates to `Range.WithinRange` instead of reimplementing it.\r\n- `ops/internal/manage`: `ReviewPeriodChecker` reads the delays of every chain with an `EthLockboxProxy` over the superchain's L1 RPC and fails on out-of-range values or on any difference between chains sharing a lockbox. All three delays are compared, matching `OPContractsManagerMigrator._validateSharedDelays`. The DelayedWETH is resolved from `SystemConfig.delayedWETH()` because `addresses.json` has no `DelayedWETHProxy` for permissioned-only chains.\r\n- `ops/cmd/check_review_period_delays`, a `just check-review-period-delays` recipe, a `check-review-period-delays` CircleCI job on PRs and a copy in the daily scheduled workflow, since delays change through superchain-ops tasks rather than registry PRs.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\n- Today all 8 lockbox chains are on distinct lockboxes with the default delays, so the equality rule is vacuous until interop sets share a lockbox. Verified against the live registry.\r\n- The lockbox check is also run by `TestReviewPeriodChecker_actual` inside the existing `go-lint-test-ops` job, so the dedicated CI job only adds the daily run.\r\n\r\nCloses [#812](https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/812)",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-19T11:38:27Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-26T15:03:39Z",
      "additions": 546,
      "deletions": 6
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABKCh-CQ",
      "title": "ops: keep genesis files as opaque JSON",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 1384,
      "body": "Stacked on #1382 (needs its monorepo bump for `op-core/genesis`).\n\nThe registry no longer uses op-geth's genesis types: it keeps genesis files as opaque JSON, validates them with op-core, and writes op-deployer's genesis as is. Decoding through `core.Genesis` keeps only the fields the linked geth knows, and upstream go-ethereum's chain config has no OP fields (`optimism`, `regolithTime`…`jovianTime`, `bedrockBlock`), so on upstream geth these would be dropped silently from every genesis the registry publishes.\n\n- `ReadGenesis`/`WriteGenesis` (used by `sync_staging`) keep the genesis JSON byte for byte. `TestGenesisRoundTrip` round-trips every file under `superchain/extra/genesis` and checks the bytes are unchanged; some files are pretty-printed, so a decode and re-encode would not keep them.\n- `ValidateGenesisIntegrity` builds an `op-core/params.ChainConfig` from the chain's TOML and compares `op-core/genesis.ToBlock().Hash()` instead of hand-building an op-geth config. Every chain `check_genesis_integrity` checks still matches its hash. op-core rejects `stateHash`, which only the legacy-migrated chains the check already skips use.\n- `create_config` writes `op-deployer inspect genesis` output compacted, which keeps its key order (go-ethereum's `core.Genesis` order). This drops `opaqueToGenesis` and its losslessness check. Unlike before, an old op-deployer's `terminalTotalDifficultyPassed` is kept and op-geth's `\"slotNumber\":null` is no longer added.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T14:05:04Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-27T09:12:02Z",
      "additions": 185,
      "deletions": 201
    },
